ints→services→repos), Celery+RabbitMQ RPC, PostgreSQL+Alembic. Built-in observability and quality (metrics, idempotency, Black, mypy, pre-commit). Cursor rules keep AI-generated code aligned so you extend without fighting the structure."},"features":{"zh":["API-only结构","分层结构（端点、服务、存储库）","Celery和RabbitMQ的RPC支持","PostgreSQL和Alembic的数据库支持","内置的可观察性和质量保证"],"ja":["API-only構造","層構造（エンドポイント、サービス、リポジトリ）","CeleryとRabbitMQのRPCサポート","PostgreSQLとAlembicのデータベースサポート","ビルトインの観測可能性と品質保証"],"ko":["API 전용 구조","계층 구조（엔드 포인트, 서비스, 리포지토리）","Celery 및 RabbitMQ의 RPC 지원","PostgreSQL 및 Alembic의 데이터베이스 지원","내장형 관찰 가능성 및 품질 보증"],"es":["Plantilla de backend de producción","Capas de endpoints, servicios y repositorios","Soporte para Celery y RabbitMQ","Base de datos PostgreSQL con Alembic","Observabilidad y calidad incorporadas"],"fr":["Modèle de backend de production","Couches d''endpoints, de services et de répositories","Prise en charge de Celery et RabbitMQ","Base de données PostgreSQL avec Alembic","Observabilité et qualité intégrées"],"de":["Produktions-Backend-Vorlage","Schichten von Endpoints, Diensten und Repositories","Unterstützung für Celery und RabbitMQ","PostgreSQL-Datenbank mit Alembic","Integrierte Observability und Qualität"],"pt":["Modelo de backend de produção com FastAPI","Camadas de endpoints, serviços e repositórios","Integração com Celery e RabbitMQ","Suporte a PostgreSQL e Alembic","Ferramentas de observabilidade e qualidade"],"ru":["Шаблон бэкенда для производства с FastAPI","Уровни конечных точек, сервисов и репозиториев","Интеграция с Celery и RabbitMQ","Поддержка PostgreSQL и Alembic","Инструменты для наблюдения и качества"],"ar":["قالب خلفية الإنتاج باستخدام FastAPI","طبقات من نقاط النهاية والخدمات والمخازن","التكامل مع Celery و RabbitMQ","دعم PostgreSQL و Alembic","أدوات للمراقبة والجودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["FastAPI最佳实践","AI工具开发","后端应用构建","Celery和RabbitMQ","PostgreSQL和Alembic","API设计","如何使用FastAPI","FastAPI教程"],"ja":["FastAPIベストプラクティス","AIエージェント開発","バックエンドアプリケーション構築","CeleryとRabbitMQ","PostgreSQLとAlembic","API設計","FastAPIの使い方","FastAPIチュートリアル"],"ko":["FastAPI 최적화 방법","AI 에이전트 개발","백엔드 애플리케이션 구축","Celery 및 RabbitMQ","PostgreSQL 및 Alembic","API 설계","FastAPI 사용법","FastAPI 튜토리얼"],"es":["herramientas de ai","fastapi","mejores prácticas","backend de producción","observabilidad","calidad","celery","rabbitmq","postgresql","alembic"],"fr":["outils ai","fastapi","meilleures pratiques","backend de production","observabilité","qualité","celery","rabbitmq","postgresql","alembic"],"de":["ai-tools","fastapi","best practices","produktions-backend","observability","qualität","celery","rabbitmq","postgresql","alembic"],"pt":["como usar FastAPI","o que é FastAPI","FastAPI vs Flask","FastAPI alternative","instalar FastAPI","guia de configuração do FastAPI","desenvolvimento de backend com FastAPI","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать FastAPI","что такое FastAPI","FastAPI vs Flask","FastAPI альтернатива","установить FastAPI","руководство по настройке FastAPI","разработка бэкенда с FastAPI","ИИ Агенты для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام FastAPI","ما هو FastAPI","FastAPI مقابل Flask","بديل FastAPI","تثبيت FastAPI","دليل إعداد FastAPI","تطوير الخلفية باستخدام FastAPI","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين"]}},"owner":"vimalkodoth","repo":"fastapi-cursor-starterkit","repoPath":"vimalkodoth/fastapi-cursor-starterkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.909Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fastapi-best-practices","description":"FastAPI standards and best practices for this project. Use when adding or changing API routes, services, dependencies, or middleware so the team follows the same patterns and conventions.","bodyPreview":"## In this repository\n\n- **Scope:** FastAPI app lives in `backend/`. Python also in `services/`; same style applies. After edits run **`make format`** and **`make lint`** from repo root.\n- **Rules:** `.cursor/rules/fastapi-python-best-practices.md`, `.cursor/rules/fastapi-patterns.md`, `.cursor/rules/standards.md`, `.cursor/rules/project.md`.\n- Full context: `.cursor/skills/README.md`.\n\n---\n\n# FastAPI best practices (team standards)\n\nStandards derived from this project’s implementation. Follow t","body":"## In this repository\n\n- **Scope:** FastAPI app lives in `backend/`. Python also in `services/`; same style applies. After edits run **`make format`** and **`make lint`** from repo root.\n- **Rules:** `.cursor/rules/fastapi-python-best-practices.md`, `.cursor/rules/fastapi-patterns.md`, `.cursor/rules/standards.md`, `.cursor/rules/project.md`.\n- Full context: `.cursor/skills/README.md`.\n\n---\n\n# FastAPI best practices (team standards)\n\nStandards derived from this project’s implementation. Follow these so the codebase stays consistent and maintainable.\n\n## 1. Project structure and layers\n\n- **Endpoints (controllers):** `backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/` — one file per domain (e.g. `data.py`, `database.py`, `metrics.py`). Only HTTP concerns: parse request, call service/repo via `Depends`, return response or raise `HTTPException`. Use **command** service for write operations (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) and **query** service for read operations (GET). See `.cursor/rules/cqrs.md`.\n- **Business logic:** `backend/app/services/` — use **command** services for writes and **query** services for reads (CQRS). Services receive repositories via constructor; use `AsyncSession` for DB when in the API path. No raw request/response objects.\n- **Data access:** `backend/app/repositories/` — use **write** repositories (create/update/delete) and **read** repositories (get/list) per domain. Repositories receive `AsyncSession`; perform queries and commits. No business rules.\n- **Shared dependencies:** `backend/app/api/v1/deps.py` — define `get_*` functions that return service or repository instances (injecting `get_async_session`). Use these in route handlers via `Depends(...)`.\n- **Models:** `backend/app/models/database.py` (SQLModel table models), `backend/app/models/schemas.py` (Pydantic request/response). DB name is **fastapi_db**.\n\n**Do not:** Put SQL or business logic in endpoint files; put HTTP logic in services or repositories.\n\n## 2. Routers and API design\n\n- Use **APIRouter** with a **prefix** and **tags** for OpenAPI grouping:\n  ```python\n  router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/data\", tags=[\"data\"])\n  ```\n- Mount routers in `backend/app/api/v1/__init__.py` on the v1 router (`prefix=\"/api/v1\"`).\n- Prefer **explicit `response_model`** and **status_code** on route decorators:\n  ```python\n  @router.post(\"/process\", response_model=TaskResult, status_code=200)\n  async def process_data(request: DataRequest, service: DataService = Depends(get_data_service)) -> TaskResult:\n  ```\n- Use **async def** for handlers that do I/O (DB, external calls). Use **def** only for handlers that do no I/O (e.g. simple metrics that read in-memory state).\n- Document with short **docstrings** on each route; they appear in OpenAPI.\n\n## 3. Dependencies (Depends)\n\n- **Session:** Use `get_async_session` from `app.core.database` for any route or dependency that touches the DB. Never create a raw engine or session in an endpoint.\n- **Services and repositories:** Define factory functions in `app.api.v1.deps` that depend on `get_async_session` and return a service or repository instance. Use them in endpoints via `Depends(get_data_service)`, `Depends(get_task_repository)`, etc.\n\nExample (from `deps.py`):\n\n```python\ndef get_data_service(session: AsyncSession = Depends(get_async_session)) -> DataService:\n    \"\"\"Dependency that returns a DataService instance (async session).\"\"\"\n    return DataService(session)\n```\n\n- In endpoints, inject the **service** (or repository when the endpoint only needs data access) and call methods; do not instantiate services or repos inside the route.\n\n## 4. Request and response models\n\n- **Request bodies:** Use Pydantic models from `app.models.schemas` (e.g. `DataRequest`). Declare them as the route parameter; FastAPI validates and parses.\n- **Responses:** Use Pydantic response models (e.g. `TaskResult`, `RecordResponse`, `TaskLogResponse`) and set `response_model=` on the decorator. **Never** return a SQLModel/ORM instance directly; map to a schema and return that (e.g. `RecordResponse.model_validate(r)` or `RecordResponse(**record)`).\n- Prefer **model_validate(orm_instance)** (Pydantic v2) when building response models from ORM objects.\n\n## 5. Async in the request path\n\n- Use **async def** for route handlers that perform I/O (DB, HTTP, etc.). Use **AsyncSession** and async repository methods so the event loop is not blocked.\n- If you must call a **blocking** operation (e.g. sync RabbitMQ RPC), run it in a thread pool with **`await asyncio.to_thread(blocking_func, ...)`** and keep the rest of the flow async (e.g. DB write). See `DataService.process_data_sync_and_save` in `app.services.data_service`.\n- Sync engine/session are only for **Celery tasks** and **startup** (e.g. `init_db`). Do not use them in request handlers.\n\n## 6. Error handling\n\n- **API boundary:** Use **HTTPException** with the appropriate status code (400, 404, 503, etc.) and a clear `detail`. Do not let uncaught exceptions bubble to the client without mapping.\n- **Services/repositories:** Raise domain-friendly exceptions or return `None`/result; let the **endpoint** translate to HTTP (e.g. `if not record: raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Record not found\")`).\n- **External calls:** When a dependency (e.g. `call_service_via_rabbitmq`) raises `ValueError`, catch it in the endpoint and map to `HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=str(e))` (or another suitable code).\n- Handle errors and edge cases **first** (early returns, guard clauses); keep the happy path last. See `.cursor/rules/error-handling.md`.\n\n## 7. Middleware and app setup\n\n- **CORS:** Configure in `main.py` (e.g. `CORSMiddleware`). Keep origins/methods/headers explicit for production.\n- **Idempotency:** Optional `Idempotency-Key` header on POST endpoints that support it; implemented in middleware (`IdempotencyMiddleware`). Do not duplicate idempotency logic in services. Paths are listed in the middleware (e.g. `/api/v1/data/process`, `/api/v1/data/process-async`).\n- **Startup:** For simple one-off init (e.g. `init_db()`), `@app.on_event(\"startup\")` is acceptable. For multi-step startup/shutdown, prefer a **lifespan** context manager.\n\n## 8. Database (PostgreSQL, SQLModel, Alembic)\n\n- **In routes:** Always use **async** session via `get_async_session` and pass it to services/repositories. Use connection pooling (already configured in `app.core.database`).\n- **Repositories:** Accept `AsyncSession` in the constructor; use `await session.commit()`, `await session.refresh(record)` after writes; use `select(Model).where(...)` and `await session.execute()` / `session.get()` for reads. Avoid N+1; batch or eager load when needed.\n- **Migrations:** Add or change models in `app.models.database`; then from `backend/` run `alembic revision --autogenerate -m \"description\"` and `alembic upgrade head`. Do not change the database name from **fastapi_db**.\n\n## 9. Naming and style\n\n- **Files and modules:** Lowercase with underscores (e.g. `data_service.py`, `task_repository.py`, `data.py` for the data router).\n- **Routers:** Name the router variable `router`. Group related routes in one file (e.g. all `/data/*` in `data.py`).\n- **Schemas:** Clear names for request (e.g. `DataRequest`) and response (e.g. `TaskResult`, `RecordResponse`). Use type hints and optional fields where appropriate.\n- **Docstrings:** Short module docstring and route docstrings so OpenAPI and readers understand purpose. Document parameters and return values in Pydantic models if non-obvious.\n\n## 10. Team checklist (before merging)\n\n- [ ] New routes live under `backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/` and are mounted in `api/v1/__init__.py`.\n- [ ] Handlers use `Depends(get_async_session)` or `Depends(get_*_service)` / `Depends(get_*_repository)` from `deps.py`; no ad-hoc session or service creation in routes.\n- [ ] Request/response use Pydantic models from `schemas.py`; responses use `response_model=` and never return raw ORM instances.\n- [ ] I/O in the request path is **async** (AsyncSession, async repo methods); any blocking call is wrapped in `asyncio.to_thread`.\n- [ ] Errors are mapped to **HTTPException** in endpoints; services/repos do not raise HTTP-specific errors.\n- [ ] New or changed DB models have an Alembic migration; DB name remains **fastapi_db**.\n- [ ] `make format` and `make lint` have been run from repo root and pass.\n\n## Quick reference (this project)\n\n| Concern | Where / how |\n|--------|-------------|\n| Add route | `backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/<domain>.py` + include in `api/v1/__init__.py` |\n| Add dependency | `backend/app/api/v1/deps.py` (e.g. `get_*_service`, `get_*_repository`) |\n| Request/response models | `backend/app/models/schemas.py` |\n| DB models | `backend/app/models/database.py` + Alembic migration |\n| Business logic | `backend/app/services/` (accept session/repos in constructor) |\n| Data access | `backend/app/repositories/` (accept AsyncSession) |\n| Blocking in request path | `await asyncio.to_thread(sync_func, ...)` then continue async |\n| Idempotency | Middleware; add path to `IDEMPOTENT_PATHS` if needed |\n\nFor more detail, see `.cursor/rules/fastapi-python-best-practices.md` and `.cursor/rules/standards.md`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:00:29.091Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Analysis Agents needing advanced FastAPI development best practices.","zh":"适合需要高级 FastAPI 开发最佳实践的 Python 分析代理。","ja":"Python 分析エージェントが高度な FastAPI 開発のベストプラクティスを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 FastAPI 개발 모범 사례가 필요한 Python 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de Python que necesitan prácticas de desarrollo avanzadas de FastAPI.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse Python ayant besoin de meilleures pratiques de développement FastAPI avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Analyseagenten, die fortgeschrittene FastAPI-Entwicklungsbest-Practices benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise Python que precisam de práticas de desenvolvimento avançadas do FastAPI.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа Python, которым необходимы передовые практики разработки FastAPI.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التحليلية بايثون الذين يحتاجون إلى ممارسات متقدمة لتطوير FastAPI."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop high-quality FastAPI applications using best practices such as layered architecture, Celery+RabbitMQ RPC, and PostgreSQL+Alembic. It provides built-in observability and quality metrics, idempotency, and code alignment using Cursor rules.","zh":"赋予代理开发高质量的 FastAPI 应用程序的能力，使用诸如分层架构、Celery+RabbitMQ RPC 和 PostgreSQL+Alembic 之类的最佳实践。它提供了内置的可观察性和质量指标、幂等性以及使用 Cursor 规则的代码对齐。","ja":"エージェントが分層アーキテクチャ、Celery+RabbitMQ RPC、PostgreSQL+Alembic などのベストプラクティスを使用して、高品質の FastAPI アプリケーションを開発する能力を提供します。内蔵の可観測性と品質メトリクス、幂等性、および Cursor ルールを使用したコードの整列を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 계층형 아키텍처, Celery+RabbitMQ RPC 및 PostgreSQL+Alembic와 같은 모범 사례를 사용하여 고품질의 FastAPI 애플리케이션을 개발할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다. 내장형 관찰 가능성 및 품질 메트릭, 멱등성 및 Cursor 규칙을 사용한 코드 정렬을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a desarrollar aplicaciones FastAPI de alta calidad utilizando las mejores prácticas, como arquitectura en capas, Celery+RabbitMQ RPC y PostgreSQL+Alembic. Proporciona observabilidad y métricas de calidad incorporadas, idempotencia y alineación de código utilizando reglas del Cursor.","fr":"Habilite les agents à développer des applications FastAPI de haute qualité en utilisant les meilleures pratiques telles que l''architecture en couches, Celery+RabbitMQ RPC et PostgreSQL+Alembic. Il fournit une observabilité et des métriques de qualité intégrées, l''idempotence et l''alignement du code à l''aide de règles de Curseur.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, hochwertige FastAPI-Anwendungen unter Verwendung von Best-Practices wie schichtarchitektur, Celery+RabbitMQ-RPC und PostgreSQL+Alembic zu entwickeln. Bietet integrierte Beobachtbarkeit und Qualitätsmetriken, Idempotenz und Codeausrichtung unter Verwendung von Cursor-Regeln.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver aplicações FastAPI de alta qualidade usando as melhores práticas, como arquitetura em camadas, Celery+RabbitMQ RPC e PostgreSQL+Alembic. Ele fornece observabilidade e métricas de qualidade integradas, idempotência e alinhamento de código usando regras do Cursor.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью разработки приложений FastAPI высокого качества с использованием передовых практик, таких как многослойная архитектура, Celery+RabbitMQ RPC и PostgreSQL+Alembic. Он предоставляет встроенную наблюдаемость и метрики качества, идемпотентность и выравнивание кода с помощью правил Cursor.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تطوير تطبيقات FastAPI عالية الجودة باستخدام أفضل الممارسات مثل الهندسة المعمارية الطبقية و Celery+RabbitMQ RPC و PostgreSQL+Alembic. إنه يوفر مراقبة مدمجة وأداء متريكة وتماسك وتراصف رمز باستخدام قواعد Cursor."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating FastAPI application development","Generating high-quality API endpoints","Debugging FastAPI applications using built-in observability"],"zh":["自动化 FastAPI 应用程序开发","生成高质量的 API 端点","使用内置可观察性调试 FastAPI 应用程序"],"ja":["FastAPI アプリケーションの自動化","高品質の API エンドポイントの生成","内蔵の可観測性を使用した FastAPI アプリケーションのデバッグ"],"ko":["FastAPI 애플리케이션 개발 자동화","고품질의 API 엔드포인트 생성","내장형 관찰 가능성을 사용한 FastAPI 애플리케이션 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización del desarrollo de aplicaciones FastAPI","Generación de puntos de conexión de API de alta calidad","Depuración de aplicaciones FastAPI utilizando la observabilidad incorporada"],"fr":["Automatisation du développement d''applications FastAPI","Génération de points de terminaison d''API de haute qualité","Débogage des applications FastAPI à l''aide de l''observabilité intégrée"],"de":["Automatisierung der FastAPI-Anwendungs-Entwicklung","Erzeugung hochwertiger API-Endpunkte","Fehlersuche in FastAPI-Anwendungen unter Verwendung der integrierten Beobachtbarkeit"],"pt":["Automatizar o desenvolvimento de aplicações FastAPI","Gerar pontos de extremidade de API de alta qualidade","Depurar aplicações FastAPI usando a observabilidade integrada"],"ru":["Автоматизация разработки приложений FastAPI","Генерация высококачественных конечных точек API","Отладка приложений FastAPI с помощью встроенной наблюдаемости"],"ar":["تأتمة تطوير تطبيقات FastAPI","إنتاج نهايات API عالية الجودة","تصحيح أخطاء تطبيقات FastAPI باستخدام المراقبة المدمجة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3.7+ only","FastAPI only","PostgreSQL+Alembic required"],"zh":["需要 Python 3.7+ 以上","仅限 FastAPI","需要 PostgreSQL+Alembic"],"ja":["Python 3.7+ 以上が必要","FastAPI のみ","PostgreSQL+Alembic が必要"],"ko":["Python 3.7+ 이상 필요","FastAPI만 해당","PostgreSQL+Alembic 필요"],"es":["Requiere solo Python 3.7+","Solo FastAPI","Se requiere PostgreSQL+Alembic"],"fr":["Nécessite uniquement Python 3.7+","FastAPI uniquement","PostgreSQL+Alembic requis"],"de":["Erfordert nur Python 3.7+","Nur FastAPI","PostgreSQL+Alembic erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige Python 3.7+ apenas","Apenas FastAPI","PostgreSQL+Alembic obrigatório"],"ru":["Требуется Python 3.7+ только","Только FastAPI","PostgreSQL+Alembic обязательный"],"ar":["يتطلب Python 3.7+ فقط","FastAPI فقط","PostgreSQL+Alembic مطلوب"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"84de07efcba56c9deffc519c852b8ca68c4d29e926c4cb2c418831a7ee3e20e6","qualityScore":39}');
